     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Chelate adults with symptoms plus PbB > 70 mcg/dL, and children with encephalopathy or PbB > 45 mcg/dL; remove the lead source first, and don't chelate during ongoing exposure."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Encephalopathy: dimercaprol 75 mg/m2 IM every 4 hours + CaNa2EDTA 1000-1500 mg/m2/day IV; give dimercaprol at least 4 hours before the first EDTA dose (prevents lead moving into the brain)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "No encephalopathy: usually succimer 10 mg/kg orally every 8 hours for 5 days, then every 12 hours for 14 days; if symptomatic, dimercaprol 50 mg/m2 IM every 4 hours + CaNa2EDTA 1000 mg/m2/day IV for 5 days instead."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Dimercaprol: contraindicated with peanut allergy; can cause hemolysis in G6PD deficiency; don't give with iron supplements."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CaNa2EDTA: confirm urine flow first; dose-related, usually reversible renal toxicity; thrombophlebitis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Succimer: rash, GI upset, metallic taste, transient liver enzyme rise."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
